<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">García Sánchez of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1009">1009</a>–<a href="/years/1029">1029</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">García Sánchez was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from 1017 to 1029, succeeding his father Sancho García as a child. He was murdered in León in 1029 by members of the Vela family on the eve of his marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancha-of-leon">Sancha of León</a>. His sister Muniadona was married to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-iii-of-navarre">Sancho III of Navarre</a>, who took control of Castile, and their son Ferdinand I later became king of Castile and León.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/garcia-sanchez-of-castile.jpg" alt="García Sánchez of Castile" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murder_of_Garc%C3%ADa_S%C3%A1nchez_of_Castile_in_1029.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the murder of the last count, <b>García Sánchez</b>, in 1029, Castile passed to Sancho III the Great of Navarre, who gave it to his son Ferdinand.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The murder of the young Count <b>García Sánchez</b> in 1029 brought Castile under Sancho III of Navarre, whose son Ferdinand I ruled it and became king of León in 1037.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-castile">County of Castile</a></li></ul></section>
